---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Terms & Conditions — BlackWhitePDF";
const description =
  "Terms and Conditions for using BlackWhitePDF, the free online grayscale PDF and black and white PDF converter.";
const path = "/terms/";
const updated = "August 8, 2026";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: title,
  description,
  url: new URL(path, Astro.site ?? "https://blackwhitepdf.com").href,
  dateModified: "2026-08-08",
  isPartOf: {
    "@type": "WebSite",
    name: "BlackWhitePDF",
    url: new URL("/", Astro.site ?? "https://blackwhitepdf.com").href,
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  current="terms"
  keywords="blackwhitepdf terms, terms and conditions, grayscale pdf converter terms"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <main id="main" class="scroll-mt-4 border-b border-hairline bg-canvas">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
      <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-mute">Legal</p>
      <h1
        class="text-[34px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-1.4px] text-balance md:text-[40px] md:tracking-[-1.8px]"
      >
        Terms &amp; Conditions.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mute">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
        These Terms &amp; Conditions (“Terms”) govern your access to and use of the
        BlackWhitePDF website and converter (the “Service”). By using the Service, you agree
        to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">1. The Service</h2>
        <p>
          BlackWhitePDF provides a free, browser-based tool to convert PDFs to grayscale PDF
          or black and white PDF, including optional crop/deskew and quality controls. The
          Service is offered “as is” for personal and professional use subject to these Terms.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">2. Eligibility</h2>
        <p>
          You must be able to form a binding contract under applicable law to use the
          Service. If you use the Service on behalf of an organization, you represent that
          you have authority to bind that organization to these Terms.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">3. Your content and responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          You retain all rights to the PDFs and other files you process. You are solely
          responsible for ensuring you have the legal right to convert, modify, download,
          and use those files. Do not use the Service to process content that is illegal,
          infringing, or that you are not authorized to handle.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because conversion runs in your browser, you are also responsible for keeping
          downloaded outputs and for verifying that results meet your quality, print, or
          archival needs before relying on them.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">4. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload, scrape abusively, or reverse engineer the Service except as allowed by law.</li>
          <li>Use the Service to distribute malware or to violate others’ privacy or intellectual property rights.</li>
          <li>Misrepresent the Service as providing server-side document storage or guaranteed OCR accuracy.</li>
          <li>Bypass rate limits, security controls, or access restrictions if implemented.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">5. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The website design, branding, copy, and software that make up the Service are
          owned by us or our licensors. You may not copy, modify, or redistribute our
          branding or site code except as permitted by applicable open-source licenses
          included with third-party libraries, or with our prior written consent.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">6. No professional advice</h2>
        <p>
          Output from the converter is a technical transformation of your file. It is not
          legal, medical, archival, or print-compliance advice. You are responsible for
          checking the downloaded PDF before filing, printing, or publishing.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">7. Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may modify, suspend, or discontinue any part of the Service at any time,
          including free features, without liability. We may also update these Terms; the
          “Last updated” date will change when we do. Continued use after an update
          constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">8. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE” WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY
          KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
          PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. We do not warrant that conversion
          will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that every page will look perfect for every
          input file.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">9. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WE AND OUR AFFILIATES WILL NOT BE LIABLE
          FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY
          LOSS OF DATA, PROFITS, OR BUSINESS, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE SERVICE. OUR
          TOTAL LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM RELATED TO THE SERVICE WILL NOT EXCEED THE GREATER
          OF THE AMOUNT YOU PAID US FOR THE SERVICE IN THE TWELVE MONTHS BEFORE THE CLAIM
          OR ONE HUNDRED U.S. DOLLARS (US&nbsp;$100). Some jurisdictions do not allow certain
          limitations; in those cases, our liability is limited to the fullest extent
          permitted.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">10. Indemnity</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to indemnify and hold us harmless from claims, damages, losses, and
          expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising from your use of the Service,
          your files, or your violation of these Terms or applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">11. Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our handling of information is described in the
          <a href="/privacy/" class="text-link underline hover:text-link-deep">Privacy Policy</a>,
          which is incorporated by reference into these Terms.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">12. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws applicable in the jurisdiction where the
          site operator is established, without regard to conflict-of-law rules, unless
          mandatory consumer protections in your country provide otherwise. Courts in that
          jurisdiction will have exclusive venue for disputes, subject to applicable
          consumer rights.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">13. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms? Reach us through our
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-link underline hover:text-link-deep">Contact</a> page,
          or see the <a href="/about/" class="text-link underline hover:text-link-deep">About Us</a> page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
